          text: "The air jet is deflected in and out of the embouchure hole by the sound wave in the tube, which sustains the oscillation. Because the tube is effectively open at both ends, its resonances form a complete harmonic series and the flute overblows the octave [1][2]. The player changes register and colour mainly by jet speed, jet length and lip coverage. Faster jets select higher resonances, and the harmonic content rises with blowing pressure [1][3].",
