          "Historical/critical: jazz musicians adopted the flute relatively late. Eric Dolphy's wide-interval, bird-like flute and Yusef Lateef's flute on 'world'-influenced records broadened its expressive palette. Charles Lloyd's flute made it a vehicle for meditative and psychedelic moods [6].",
