          text: "A drumhead vibrates in many modes whose frequencies are inharmonic (not whole-number multiples). Drums therefore have a vague rather than definite pitch, set mainly by head tension and diameter, and the shell and enclosed air couple to the head modes [1][2]. Cymbals are thin bronze plates that vibrate nonlinearly when struck hard. Energy cascades in the first milliseconds from low modes into hundreds of high, closely spaced modes, giving a broadband, shimmering spectrum [2][3].",
