          "Historical/critical: Baby Dodds brought New Orleans drumming to record, and Jo Jones moved the time to the hi-hat in Basie's band. Kenny Clarke shifted it to the ride cymbal, freeing the bass drum for accents ('dropping bombs'), and Philly Joe Jones and Elvin Jones made the drummer an equal, conversational storyteller. Elvin's polyrhythmic triplet layers with Coltrane are often described as a 'cloud' of rhythm rather than a beat [8].",
